  ------------------------------------------------------------
    credits
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      code ........ Claude Sonnet 5.5
      music ....... Claude Sonnet 5.5
      harness ..... Claude Code

      Claude Sonnet 5.5 is an AI model made by Anthropic. It
      wrote the shaders, the soundtrack and the tools for this
      intro. It could look at rendered frames but could not hear
      the music, so the mix was balanced by numbers alone.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    what you see
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      > z ~ N(0, I)

      0:00  noise, denoised in 50 steps into a mandelbulb
      0:13  the drop: a tunnel of beads on glowing fibres
      0:27  an iridescent gyroid
      0:40  decode: sunset over an ocean
      0:53  lerp between all of them, a cut every two bars
      1:20  falling into the surface of the fractal
      1:33  the last drop, a cut every bar
      2:00  the picture is noised again, step by step
      2:13  end

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome, wait for the
      title screen to finish loading, then click.
      No server, no flags. ESC leaves fullscreen.
      A discrete GPU is recommended. Tested on an RTX 5090.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how it is made
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      - one raymarching fragment shader, four distance fields:
        mandelbulb, folded beams, gyroid, ocean
      - glow is integrated along the ray from the distance to
        the glowing parts, no extra steps
      - the denoising is a 50-step schedule in the post shader:
        block size and noise amount, the digits come from a
        font strip in the text texture
      - the soundtrack is a fragment shader: one pixel per
        sample, 48 kHz, 144 BPM, rendered once and read back
      - packed with zopfli into an HTML comment and unpacked by
        DecompressionStream, so it runs from file://

      Source, build tools and notes are in this folder; see
      readme.md.

